 {:name "switch-to-setIntegral-mono-on-for-cell-local-bounds"
  :lane :arc-lane
  :level :api-selection
  :status :draft
  :body
  {:scope
   {:language :lean4
    :context
    "The Darboux infimum/supremum bounds are known only for points belonging to the current partition cell."}
   :before
   "Apply `setIntegral_mono`, which asks for a global pointwise inequality and does not consume the available cell-membership hypothesis in the needed form."
   :after
   "Apply `setIntegral_mono_on` with integrability of both integrands and `measurableSet_Icc`, then discharge its comparison using the local `x ∈ cell` bound."
   :rule
   "When the comparison is inherently restricted to the set being integrated over, select the `_on` monotonicity theorem rather than strengthening a local bound into an unnecessary global one."
   :capture-kind :runner-error-fix-log-and-commit-witnessed}
